---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { SITE_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<LegalPage title="Refund Policy" description="Refund and cancellation terms for iswar.me subscriptions and services.">
	<p>This Refund Policy applies to subscriptions for software provided by OneMBCo through iswar.me. Paddle is the Merchant of Record for transactions processed through Paddle.</p>

	<h2>1. Cancellation</h2>
	<p>You may cancel your subscription at any time by emailing <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>. Cancellation stops future renewals. You will normally retain access through the end of the current paid billing period.</p>

	<h2>2. First-payment refunds</h2>
	<p>If you are not satisfied with a subscription, you may request a refund of your first payment within 14 days of the original purchase. You can request it directly through <a href="https://paddle.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">paddle.net</a> by selecting “Request refund,” or contact us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a> with the account email and payment details so we can help locate the transaction.</p>

	<h2>3. Renewals and billing errors</h2>
	<p>Renewal payments are generally non-refundable once the billing period has started. We will review requests for duplicate charges, incorrect charges, or service access problems and issue an appropriate refund when the charge was made in error.</p>

	<h2>4. How refunds are paid</h2>
	<p>Approved refunds are sent through Paddle to the original payment method. Paddle is the Merchant of Record for transactions processed through its platform and handles payment support and refund processing. Processing times depend on your bank or card provider. A refund does not automatically cancel a subscription, so please request cancellation as well if you do not want future renewals.</p>

	<h2>5. Contact</h2>
	<p>For refund or cancellation help, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>. We aim to respond within three business days.</p>
</LegalPage>
